# `%r1.h0` selects the low half of %r1, and the `vadd` writes all of
# %r1, so the address after it is not the thread index's; it was read as
# `4 * %tid.x + param_0` where ptxas stores to param_0 from all 32 threads.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/video_selector.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_video_selector
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B {{ +}}unknown: depends on special register %tid.x, behind `vadd.u32.u32.u32`
